{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9e6a0de6-6c5a-4ccb-9887-1a9e871b0d3a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8795dd3b8afbc1fb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9018-b1jg5z7f/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9018-E001.md","content":"# Per-project GPU-hour consumption reporting with stable API and CSV export\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the core administrator-facing chargeback reporting\ncapability: per-project GPU-hour consumption reports computed over selectable\ntime ranges from the per-project usage data delivered by the in-flight GPU\nusage metering strategy (RHAISTRAT-9990). Reports are exposed through a stable\nAPI for finance tooling and exportable as CSV. This epic consumes the metering\ndata; it does not re-implement the metering collection pipeline.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Compute per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable time ranges,\n  reading the per-project GPU-hour usage data delivered by the GPU usage\n  metering strategy.\n- Expose the reports through a stable, documented API suitable for finance\n  tooling retrieval.\n- Provide CSV export of the reports.\n- Define and apply consistent GPU-hour aggregation semantics (what counts as a\n  GPU-hour, how usage aggregates over the selected time range) across the API\n  and CSV outputs.\n- Reside in the Distributed Workloads stack: the Dashboard owns no data plane,\n  so the report computation and delivery surface belong to this component.\n\nOut of scope: the metering collection pipeline itself (owned by the metering\nstrategy), and currency/cost-rate modelling — reports are in GPU-hours, not\ndollars.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given metered per-project GPU-hour usage data, an administrator can retrieve\n  a per-project consumption report for a selectable time range, and the\n  reported totals reconcile with the underlying metering data for that range.\n- Reports are retrievable via a stable, documented API and are exportable as\n  CSV, with both delivery modes producing consistent figures.\n- The report implementation consumes the metering data as delivered by the\n  metering strategy and, once that strategy lands its final data schema, is\n  validated against the final schema — any divergence is reconciled in the\n  report implementation without re-implementing collection.\n- The GPU-hour aggregation semantics used by the reports are implemented\n  deterministically and identically across the API and CSV outputs.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)**: per-project GPU-hour consumption reports over selectable\n  time ranges computed from the metering data — fully covered by this epic.\n- **HLR-2 (P1)**: CSV export and stable API retrieval for finance tooling —\n  covered by this epic. Bundled with the P0 reporting work rather than split:\n  export and API retrieval are delivery modes of the same report surface over\n  the same per-project consumption data structures, so the HLR is not\n  independently deferrable and splitting it would build the same surface twice.\n\n## Risks\n\n- The metering data schema is owned by the metering strategy and finalizes only\n  when that strategy lands; report field mappings and aggregation logic carry\n  rework risk until then. Mitigated by the schema-reconciliation acceptance\n  criterion above; implementation may proceed against the schema as currently\n  delivered.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":39723,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b464f0edfe0c1207","agent_id":"acf4d4388f6cbb2d7","session_id":"0a40a135-68eb-4401-87dc-e3c142162fc5","uuid":"5cc6cddd-10e8-4c7e-a0a5-3a5696271302","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:21:20.806Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9018"}
