 quota or admission logic, and any\n51\tre-implementation of consumption computation — the view displays figures\n52\tproduced by the reporting capability.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- An administrator can open the admin view in the Dashboard console and see,\n57\t  per project, current-month GPU-hour consumption alongside the project's\n58\t  Kueue quota.\n59\t- Projects whose current-month consumption exceeds their Kueue quota are\n60\t  clearly indicated in the view.\n61\t- The view is presented to administrator users consistent with the platform's\n62\t  authentication and RBAC model.\n63\t- Consumption figures shown in the view reconcile with the per-project\n64\t  current-month figures retrievable from the reporting capability's API.\n65\t\n66\t## HLR Traceability\n67\t\n68\t- **HLR-3 (P1)**: the Dashboard admin view shows current-month consumption\n69\t  against each project's Kueue quota — fully covered by this epic.\n70\t\n71\t## Notes\n72\t\n73\t- The Dashboard owns no data plane and speaks the Kubernetes API only (per its\n74\t  architecture context); the mechanism by which report data reaches the\n75\t  Dashboard is an implementation decision for the owning teams and is not\n76\t  prescribed here.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a62252639080d96e","agent_id":"aef3493fde2dfd87e","session_id":"0a40a135-68eb-4401-87dc-e3c142162fc5","uuid":"d8622cb9-e7cf-4ca7-a670-cf924254cd56","timestamp":"2026-10-26T12:25:58.690Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa513464c11614d8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9018 decomposition"}
